define phrase teisha-trade
  (TODO during play-testing — TE20: the necklace for the dress and the
  fashionable hat.)
end phrase

define phrase teisha-hurry
  Suddenly you hear someone shouting just outside: 'Hey, any of you dims
  check inside this tent yet?'

  Teisha's face turns white. 'Hurry, Jack!' she hisses, 'Out the back way!'
end phrase

## DAVID: TE1 opens "Change your mind about that cloak?" — a cloak Jack never
## discussed in the calm walk. Gentry's (`story.ni:3176`), kept aside:
##   "'Hello, Jack,' says Teisha. 'Change your mind about that cloak?' Then
##   she gets a look at your face and frowns. 'Something the matter, sweetie?
##   You look spooked.'"

define phrase teisha-spooked
  (TODO during play-testing — TE1 without the cloak: Teisha sees Jack's face
  and knows something is wrong.)
end phrase

define phrase teisha-back-so-soon
  'Back so soon, Jack?' Teisha asks. She eyes you closely. 'Are you sure
  there's nothing the matter?'
end phrase

define phrase teisha-still-here
  Teisha's face falls as you stumble back into the tent. 'You're still
  here?' she asks. 'I'd hoped you'd gotten away by now.'
end phrase

define phrase teisha-told-mercenaries
  'Now that you mention it, I am a bit spooked,' you say, trying to catch
  your breath. 'There's a bunch of big guys with swords out there, chasing
  me all over the market!'

  Teisha frowns. 'Big guys with — you mean mercenaries? In Grubber's?' She
  peeks out through the front flap. 'Brigid help us,' she mutters, glancing
  back at you. 'Don't tell me what they're after you for — I don't want to
  know.'
end phrase

define phrase teisha-just-tricky
  'No, really,' you say, in a not-quite-steady voice. 'Everything's just
  tricky.'

  Teisha smirks. 'Uh-huh. You know I don't just sit by myself in this silk
  tent all day, don't you, Jack? I do have some idea of what's going on in
  the world outside, you know. I know there are mercenaries searching
  Grubber's, and I'm guessing they're probably after you.' Her voice softens,
  and she puts her hand on your shoulder. 'Don't worry, Jack. I don't need
  to know what you did to get them after you. I won't turn you in.'
end phrase

define phrase teisha-hide
  'I need help, Teisha,' you tell her plaintively. 'I need somewhere to
  hide.'

  Teisha sighs. Although you know she cares about you, you also know that
  Teisha is a smart, practical woman, and first and foremost she is worried
  about losing her customers. 'All right,' she says, 'you can stay in here
  as long as you like, but if the mercenaries decide to search the place I
  can't stop them. Probably your best bet is to slip out that way—' she
  points to the narrow gap in the back wall of the tent. 'I'll pretend I
  never saw you.'
end phrase

